6","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107226","id":3802313966,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7iorTu","user":{"login":"LemmaEOF","id":6722691,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3MjI2OTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6722691?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF","html_url":"https://github.com/LemmaEOF","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-26T23:47:05Z","updated_at":"2026-02-24T23:29:11Z","body":"Are there any more blocks on this PR? It'd be huge to have once the 4.7 cycle spins up!","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3802313966/reactions","total_count":12,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":5,"rocket":0,"eyes":7},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":{"reason":"off-topic"}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3954521176","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107226#issuecomment-3954521176","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107226","id":3954521176,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7rtTRY","user":{"login":"BuzzLord","id":11238951,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjM4OTUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11238951?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord","html_url":"https://github.com/BuzzLord","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-24T20:23:59Z","updated_at":"2026-02-24T20:23:59Z","body":"@PizzaLovers007 After the discussion in the audio meeting today, I was looking at `AudioStreamSynchronized`, and thought it would be a good starting point for trying to do scheduling inside an `AudioStream`. I took a stab at it, if you want to take a look:  #116735.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3954521176/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3964310813","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107226#issuecomment-3964310813","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107226","id":3964310813,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7sSpUd","user":{"login":"PizzaLovers007","id":10912951,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwOTEyOTUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10912951?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007","html_url":"https://github.com/PizzaLovers007","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-26T06:02:14Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T06:02:14Z","body":"I think there are still a couple more things I need to address:\r\n* `get_absolute_time()` does a simple division by mix rate, which if it changes can cause the time to teleport forward/backward. Mix rate can change if the audio device changes. Unity's dspTime does not fluctuate when changing audio devices.\r\n* Silence frames are mixed for every scheduled playback, which impacts performance. Scheduling 1000 sounds in a single ScheduledAudioStreamPlayer with `max_polyphony` 1000 in an empty scene runs at ~190 FPS on my machine. Optimizing here could be done before the playbacks are added to the AudioServer, or have the AudioServer have special handling for these types of playbacks.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3964310813/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3964468648","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107226#issuecomment-3964468648","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107226","id":3964468648,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7sTP2o","user":{"login":"LemmaEOF","id":6722691,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY3MjI2OTE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6722691?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF","html_url":"https://github.com/LemmaEOF","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/LemmaEOF/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-26T06:43:25Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T06:43:25Z","body":"It'd be really nice if it was possible to go directly by sample count, but from my own experiences digging around in the audio server code that doesn't seem super feasible.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3964468648/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3966420030","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107226#issuecomment-3966420030","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107226","id":3966420030,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7sasQ-","user":{"login":"BuzzLord","id":11238951,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjM4OTUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11238951?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord","html_url":"https://github.com/BuzzLord","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/BuzzLord/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-02-26T12:48:17Z","updated_at":"2026-02-26T12:48:17Z","body":"> `get_absolute_time()` does a simple division by mix rate, which if it changes can cause the time to teleport forward/backward. Mix rate can change if the audio device changes. Unity's dspTime does not fluctuate when changing audio devices.\r\n\r\nYou could add an explicit `double absolute_time` in the audio server, updated alongside `mix_frames`. Every time `mix_frames` is updated (in `_mix_step`), update `absolute_time` by the same, divided by the current `mix_rate`. Then in `AudioStreamPlaybackScheduled`, store the actual double start time (instead of converting it to a mix frame), and when its needs to start mixing, multiply by the current mix rate to get an exact frame to begin. Doubles should have enough precision for any reasonable time frame.\r\n\r\n> Silence frames are mixed for every scheduled playback, which impacts performance. Scheduling 1000 sounds in a single ScheduledAudioStreamPlayer with `max_polyphony` 1000 in an empty scene runs at ~190 FPS on my machine. Optimizing here could be done before the playbacks are added to the AudioServer, or have the AudioServer have special handling for these types of playbacks.\r\n\r\n`AudioServer` checks playbacks to see if they are paused, and skips them entirely if they are. I think you could use this. If you could override the `AudioStreamPlayerInternal` process function somehow for the scheduled players, you could check each playback to see if its not going to start for some threshold amount of time, and pause playbacks if they're too far out, then resume them once they're close to playing.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3966420030/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4115411969","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107226#issuecomment-4115411969","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107226","id":4115411969,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc71TDQB","user":{"login":"PizzaLovers007","id":10912951,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwOTEyOTUx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10912951?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007","html_url":"https://github.com/PizzaLovers007","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/PizzaLovers007/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-24T05:01:57Z","updated_at":"2026-03-24T05:05:56Z","body":"> `AudioServer` checks playbacks to see if they are paused, and skips them entirely if they are. I think you could use this. If you could override the `AudioStreamPlayerInternal` process function somehow for the scheduled players, you could check each playback to see if its not going to start for some threshold amount of time, and pause playbacks if they're too far out, then resume them once they're close to playing.\r\n\r\nI think the pausing strategy introduces some complexities that are a bit difficult to address, especially when the player is *actually* paused, so I instead tried to move the silence frame logic back into the AudioServer. Even with optimized mixing (only mixing when < 512 frames of silence are needed), AudioStreamPlayerInternal still has an O(N^2) operation since every AudioServer method is effectively O(N). Specifically this loop+condition:\r\n\r\n```cpp\r\nvoid AudioStreamPlayerInternal::process() {\r\n\tfor (Ref<AudioStreamPlayback> &playback : stream_playbacks) {\r\n\t\tif (playback.is_valid() && !AudioServer::get_singleton()->is_playback_active(playback) && !AudioServer::get_singleton()->is_playback_paused(playback)) {\r\n\t\t\t// snip\r\n\t\t}\r\n\t}\r\n\t// ...\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis wasn't really an issue before, but with scheduled sounds, it's more likely users would run into this performance issue.\r\n\r\nI'm not very happy with the current state, but here's a draft PR of what I have: #117781. Ideally `AudioStreamPlayerScheduled` should handle the scheduling itself and only add to AudioServer once it's almost time for the playback to play.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4115411969/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5755788836","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107226#issuecomment-5755788836","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/107226","id":5755788836,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABVxJeJA","user":{"login":"wuharvey","id":6209894,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYyMDk4OTQ=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6209894?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/wuharvey","html_url":"https://github.com/wuharvey","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wuharvey/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wuharvey/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wuharvey/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wuharvey/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wuharvey/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wuharvey/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wuharvey/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wuharvey/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/wuharvey/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-09-21T05:22:58Z","updated_at":"2026-09-21T05:22:58Z","body":"Thanks for cool work here @PizzaLovers007!\r\n\r\nWanted to ask folks what needs to be done to wrap up and get this merged? I would be happy to contribute. I've been using a custom build of Godot with this code for my rhythm game, and would love to not have to deal with a custom build in the future :D ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5755788836/reactions","total_count":5,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":5,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5803739254","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107226#issueco